{"kind":"request","text":"ox-checker: independent Architecture/Security/Simplification review of exact head 18d419d2defa1dec58d6ecac4c0997343497e1dd on branch request/merge-all-live-succession (worktree /Users/hughpyle/play/gitseq-worktrees/merge-all-live-succession), implementing request #10209. The implementation report is the artifact at cmd/gs standing on that head: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:09e3407a585c0af0aaedaca139a058525cd416c8.\n\nTHE CHANGE. planSuccession no longer filters predecessors by commit reachability: successionPredecessors is deleted, and the plan is built from the verified full live projection, excluding retired records and historical dot/comma pseudo-paths. Every live pointer whose path the first-parent diff touches retires whatever commit it stands on; exact winners succeed to the single merge successor; pointers strictly beneath a winning path retire bare with the surviving wider path named in the supersession text; deleted and renamed paths retire bare. Cross-author refusal, reviewed-path bounds, the citation guard, path validation, sealed-receipt replay, idempotent retry, and refusal before HEAD moves are preserved.\n\nARCHITECTURE. Per the governing conditions, please name affected layers 5 Workroom semantics, 6 verified projection/query, and 7 CLI merge workflow, and confirm the exact head preserves their contract or that docs/reference/architecture.md is updated in the same head.\n\nSECURITY. Please examine explicitly: merge authority (approved implementer), reviewed-path bounds over the widened retirement set (cross-author refusal now meets more targets), the citation guard against newly bare retirements of cited narrow pointers, untrusted paths in the diff versus projection paths, and failure before HEAD moves.\n\nSIMPLIFICATION. The ancestry scan was deleted rather than another heuristic added; if any residual complexity can be cut without weakening conditions of satisfaction, say so.\n\nGates actually